
# ── Subject (line above): type(scope): imperative summary, <= 72 chars ─────
#   types:  feat fix refactor test docs chore ops ci perf
#   scopes: the area, not the file — auth story media search graph ai web
#           core-api infra compose helm ci docs
#
# ── Body — answer "why is this safe to merge?" ─────────────────────────────
#   Why:   the problem or motivation. What was broken or missing, and why it
#          matters. Lead with this — the diff already shows the "what".
#   How:   the approach at decision level, plus anything in the diff that
#          would surprise a reviewer (renames, moved code, config changes,
#          behavior changes hiding in "cleanup").
#   Proof: for behavior changes, what you exercised and what you observed.
#
#   Skip the body only when the subject truly says it all (typo, dep bump).
#   Wrap at 72. Never recap files changed — `git show --stat` does that.
#
# ── Trailers (last lines, one per line) ────────────────────────────────────
#   Fixes #<issue>                       auto-closes the issue on merge
#   Refs: openspec/changes/<change-id>   for spec-driven work
#   Co-Authored-By: <AI model> <noreply@anthropic.com>
